# Measured with native LAMMPS: engine vs native (b332f28, /home/roy/.local/bin/lmp, PKG REPLICA, MPI, 2 partitions) per partition: thermo max err 2.0e-14 (relative), per-atom max 1.4e-12 (108 atoms, 160 steps, about 4-6 s engine incl. node start: the eam/alloy table parse dominates, as in w21pot_eam_alloy).
# Note: the nvt damping is 0.1 ps, not the example's 0.002 ps. A Nose-Hoover period equal to the timestep amplifies rounding differences: a single-partition run of the same system with 0.002 already differs from native by 1.4e-5 (temp) at step 200 and 2% at step 300 (measured), so the example cannot be held to 1e-8.
# oracle: w194alc_alloy — fix alchemy on 2 partitions: pure fcc Cu (partition 0) and Cu with 5% Al (partition 1), the forces are mixed with lambda ramp(1,0)/ramp(0,1) and the per-partition energies, pressure/alchemy
# oracle-partitions: 2
# oracle-potentials: AlCu.eam.alloy
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-8 abs=1e-10
variable name world pure alloy
units metal
lattice fcc 3.75
region box block 0 3 0 3 0 2
create_box 2 box
timestep 0.002
create_atoms 1 box
displace_atoms all random 0.3 0.3 0.3 57845645
pair_style eam/alloy
pair_coeff * * AlCu.eam.alloy Cu Al
if "${name} == alloy" then "set type 1 type/fraction 2 0.05 6745234"
if "${name} == pure" then "variable ramp equal ramp(1.0,0.0)" else "variable ramp equal ramp(0.0,1.0)"
velocity all create 5000.0 6567345
fix 1 all nvt temp 2500.0 500.0 0.1
fix 2 all alchemy v_ramp
compute pressure all pressure/alchemy 2
thermo_style custom step temp press etotal density pe ke f_2 f_2[3]
thermo_modify press pressure
thermo_modify format float %.15g
thermo 20
run 160 post no
